---
import QuestionLayout from '@layouts/QuestionLayout.astro';

const jsonLd = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [{
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: 'Where does BundleEmbedder get runtime.wasm?',
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: 'From your app bundle. BundleEmbedder in traverse-embedder-web loads runtime/runtime.wasm plus runtime/runtime.wasm.sha256 from the bundle, verifies the digest, and fails closed at init if the file is missing. The npm package does not ship runtime.wasm. Download the artifact-only GitHub release that matches your package. For 0.17.1 that is runtime-wasm-v0.17.1 (sha256 f2b1bebe89e5a779604feecb3bae2be1f94c6e8f67ab628838e04553f259306d, bridge 1.1.0). Older matches: runtime-wasm-v0.16.2 (b313b5c5...) and runtime-wasm-v0.16.1 (7a322a17...). Each release carries runtime.wasm, runtime.wasm.sha256 and runtime-release.json.',
    },
  }],
});

const relatedLinks = [
  { href: '/questions/what-is-one-shared-runtime-wasm.html', label: 'What is one shared runtime.wasm in Traverse?' },
  { href: '/questions/does-the-rust-embedder-use-the-same-runtime-wasm.html', label: 'Does the Rust embedder use the same runtime.wasm?' },
  { href: '/questions/does-catalog-model-execute-run-on-published-traverse-packages.html', label: 'Does catalog model.execute run on published Traverse packages?' },
  { href: '/questions/how-do-i-upgrade-to-traverse-v0-16-0.html', label: 'How do I upgrade to Traverse v0.16.x?' },
];
---
<QuestionLayout
  title="Where does BundleEmbedder get runtime.wasm?"
  description="From your app bundle, digest-checked. npm traverse-embedder-web does not ship it. For 0.17.1, download runtime-wasm-v0.17.1 and check the sha256."
  canonical="https://traverse-framework.com/questions/where-does-bundleembedder-get-runtime-wasm.html"
  category="Runtime and architecture"
  relatedLinks={relatedLinks}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <p><strong>Short answer:</strong> from your app bundle. <code>BundleEmbedder</code> loads <code>runtime/runtime.wasm</code> and <code>runtime/runtime.wasm.sha256</code> from the bundle you give it, checks the digest, and fails closed at <code>init</code> if the file isn't there. To get the file, download it from the <code>runtime-wasm</code> release that matches your <code>traverse-embedder-web</code> version.</p>

  <h2>What ships where</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>npm <code>traverse-embedder-web</code></strong> does not include <code>runtime.wasm</code>. The orchestrator belongs to the app bundle.</li>
    <li><strong><a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/releases/tag/runtime-wasm-v0.17.1"><code>runtime-wasm-v0.17.1</code></a></strong> matches <code>traverse-embedder-web@0.17.1</code>. sha256 <code>f2b1bebe89e5a779604feecb3bae2be1f94c6e8f67ab628838e04553f259306d</code>, bridge 1.1.0. Checked 2026-11-16.</li>
    <li><strong><a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/releases/tag/runtime-wasm-v0.16.2"><code>runtime-wasm-v0.16.2</code></a></strong> and <strong><a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/releases/tag/runtime-wasm-v0.16.1"><code>runtime-wasm-v0.16.1</code></a></strong> are the matching assets for those package versions. Each has <code>runtime.wasm</code>, <code>runtime.wasm.sha256</code> and <code>runtime-release.json</code>. They are never marked Latest.</li>
    <li><strong>The tag still has it.</strong> <code>runtime/runtime.wasm</code> and <code>runtime/runtime-release.json</code> are committed at each release tag, with the same bytes.</li>
    <li>Before November 4 the last <code>runtime-wasm-v*</code> release was <code>runtime-wasm-v0.11.0</code>, so v0.16.0 has no matching release. Take v0.16.0 from its tag.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What to do</h2>
  <p>Download the three files for your version and check the digest before you put the file in your bundle. For v0.17.1:</p>
  <pre><code>BASE=https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/releases/download/runtime-wasm-v0.17.1
curl -fsSLO $BASE/runtime.wasm
curl -fsSLO $BASE/runtime.wasm.sha256
curl -fsSLO $BASE/runtime-release.json
sha256sum runtime.wasm
# expect f2b1bebe89e5a779604feecb3bae2be1f94c6e8f67ab628838e04553f259306d</code></pre>
  <p><code>runtime-release.json</code> for v0.17.1 reads <code>runtime_version</code> 0.17.1, <code>bridge_version</code> 1.1.0, <code>bridge_abi_version</code> 10100, and that sha256. <code>runtime.wasm.sha256</code> already holds <code>sha256:&lt;hex&gt;</code>, the form the bundle expects, so it can go straight into <code>runtime/</code>. For v0.16.2 expect <code>b313b5c5c11291d9e9669125a0a9a77aa42a911b15d431a73e86b17c874e298c</code>. For v0.16.1 expect <code>7a322a17e3fd58f8bd26e915dd81bad68732500dc981499bd280a6d2e6507d52</code>.</p>
  <p>Or build it yourself from the tagged source with Rust 1.95 or later. Either way you end up with one shared <code>runtime.wasm</code> that every web and Node host loads; native Rust hosts link <code>traverse-runtime</code> directly and don't need the file.</p>

  <h2>What changed</h2>
  <p><a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/issues/1784">traverse#1784</a> asked how apps should get the file. <a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/pull/1797">traverse#1797</a> closed it: every product tag publishes <code>runtime-wasm-vX.Y.Z</code>, and the product GitHub Release waits for it (Spec 048 1.5.0, Decision 123). v0.16.1 and v0.16.2 were backfilled. v0.17.1 published <code>runtime-wasm-v0.17.1</code> with the product release. There is no <code>runtime-wasm-v0.17.0</code> artifact. npm still does not ship the file.</p>
</QuestionLayout>
